  "worked_solution": "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nL(a{y}_{1}(x)+b{y}_{2}(x))=aL({y}_{1}(x))+bL({y}_{2}(x))\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L({y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}) & =L({y}_{1})+3L({y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-3x+3\\cdot x(x+1) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-3x+3{x}^{2}+3x \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+3{x}^{2})+(3x-3x) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}+0 \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
